DTSTART:20250809T003000Z
DTEND:20250809T020000Z
DTSTAMP:20250809T003000Z
UID:19GJWwriBC
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 70 mins (1h10m)\n\nThe world's #1 cat video festival
  is back with screenings in theaters across the USA and around the world. 
 A portion of ticket proceeds will benefit PAWS and NEKO Cat Cafe.\n\nhttp
 s://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/cat-vid-fest
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tim Travers and the Time Traveler’s Paradox
DTSTART:20250809T020000Z
DTEND:20250809T040500Z
DTSTAMP:20250809T020000Z
UID:JdbkLuxyYM
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 103 mins (1h43m)\n\nIn this blast of WA state scienc
 e fiction co-starring Felicia Day (“Mystery Science Theater 3000”)\, K
 eith David (The Thing)\, and Seattle native Joel McHale (“Community”)\
 , a brilliant scientist invents a time machine and concocts a scheme to ki
 ll his younger self…with unintended consequences.\n\nhttps://www.siff.ne
 t/cinema/in-theaters/tim-travers-and-the-time-travelers-paradox
LOCATION:SIFF Film Center\, 305 Harrison Street
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It’s Never Over\, Jeff Buckley
DTSTART:20250809T023000Z
DTEND:20250809T044000Z
DTSTAMP:20250809T023000Z
UID:kjZchP36kO
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nThe definitive tale of Jeff Buck
 ley\, the rising young star with an otherworldly voice whose sudden death 
 at age 30\, after the release of his critically acclaimed debut album "Gra
 ce\," shocked the world. Told through never-before-seen footage from Buckl
 ey’s archives and intimate accounts. Includes 26 minutes of exclusive\, 
 remastered footage from a previously unreleased solo performance filmed Fe
 bruary 19\, 1994\, screening immediately after the film:Very few were fort
 unate enough to witness Jeff Buckley live\, but those who did often descri
 bed it as transcendent\, jaw-dropping\, and emotionally shattering. As par
 t of the theatrical release of It’s Never Over: Jeff Buckley\, Magnolia 
 Pictures will proudly present 26 minutes of exclusive\, remastered footage
  from a rare solo performance at The Middle East in Cambridge\, MA\, filme
 d on February 19\, 1994. This previously unreleased set will screen immedi
 ately following the film\, offering both longtime fans and newcomers a rar
 e opportunity to experience Jeff Buckley’s raw\, unfiltered brilliance.\
 n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/its-never-over-jeff-buckley
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Throne of Blood
DTSTART:20250809T024500Z
DTEND:20250809T045500Z
DTSTAMP:20250809T024500Z
UID:JSNESVwtE7
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 109 mins (1h49m)\n\nAkira Kurosawa: A Retrospective 
 A vivid\, visceral Macbeth adaptation sets Shakespeare’s definitive tale
  of ambition and duplicity in a ghostly\, fog-enshrouded landscape in feud
 al Japan. New 4K restoration.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/
 akira-kurosawa-retrospective/throne-of-blood
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
