BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It’s Never Over\, Jeff Buckley
DTSTART:20250810T224500Z
DTEND:20250811T005500Z
DTSTAMP:20250810T224500Z
UID:d9pTMQPIIv
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nThe definitive tale of Jeff Buck
 ley\, the rising young star with an otherworldly voice whose sudden death 
 at age 30\, after the release of his critically acclaimed debut album "Gra
 ce\," shocked the world. Told through never-before-seen footage from Buckl
 ey’s archives and intimate accounts. Includes 26 minutes of exclusive\, 
 remastered footage from a previously unreleased solo performance filmed Fe
 bruary 19\, 1994\, screening immediately after the film:Very few were fort
 unate enough to witness Jeff Buckley live\, but those who did often descri
 bed it as transcendent\, jaw-dropping\, and emotionally shattering. As par
 t of the theatrical release of It’s Never Over: Jeff Buckley\, Magnolia 
 Pictures will proudly present 26 minutes of exclusive\, remastered footage
  from a rare solo performance at The Middle East in Cambridge\, MA\, filme
 d on February 19\, 1994. This previously unreleased set will screen immedi
 ately following the film\, offering both longtime fans and newcomers a rar
 e opportunity to experience Jeff Buckley’s raw\, unfiltered brilliance.\
 n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/its-never-over-jeff-buckley
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
