DTEND:20250814T015500Z
DTSTAMP:20250814T000000Z
UID:RQmuLpclLp
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 95 mins (1h35m)\n\nAkira Kurosawa: A Retrospective T
 oshiro Mifune swaggers and snarls to brilliant comic effect in Akira Kuros
 awa's tightly paced\, beautifully composed companion piece to Yojimbo. New
  4K restoration.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/akira-kurosaw
 a-retrospective/sanjuro
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:They Live
DTSTART:20250814T010000Z
DTEND:20250814T025500Z
DTSTAMP:20250814T010000Z
UID:VUDcsmrY4m
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 94 mins (1h34m)\n\nSIFF Movie Club A rugged loner (R
 oddy Piper) stumbles upon a terrifying discovery: ghoulish creatures are m
 asquerading as humans while they lull the public into submission through s
 ubliminal advertising messages.  Introduced by SIFF Cinema Assistant Mana
 ger Tony Ochoa.\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/siff-movie-clu
 b/they-live
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 1\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:High and Low
DTSTART:20250814T023000Z
DTEND:20250814T051500Z
DTSTAMP:20250814T023000Z
UID:Ue64o9ImLg
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 143 mins (2h23m)\n\nAkira Kurosawa: A Retrospective 
 Toshiro Mifune is unforgettable as Kingo Gondo\, a wealthy industrialist w
 hose family becomes the target of a cold-blooded kidnapper in this highly 
 influential domestic drama and police procedural. New 4K restoration.\n\nh
 ttps://www.siff.net/programs-and-events/akira-kurosawa-retrospective/high-
 and-low
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Downtown\, 2100 4th Avenue
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Together
DTSTART:20250814T024500Z
DTEND:20250814T045000Z
DTSTAMP:20250814T024500Z
UID:DSLEZ2jen5
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 102 mins (1h42m)\n\nYears into their relationship\, 
 Tim and Millie (Dave Franco and Alison Brie) find themselves at a crossroa
 ds as they move to the country\, abandoning all that is familiar in their 
 lives except each other. With tensions already flaring\, a nightmarish enc
 ounter with a mysterious\, unnatural force threatens to corrupt their live
 s\, their love\, and their flesh. Note: No Open Captions on July 29. "[A] 
 delightfully unhinged spin on the body horror joint."—Kate Erbland\, In
 dieWire\n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/together
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 3\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:It’s Never Over\, Jeff Buckley
DTSTART:20250814T224500Z
DTEND:20250815T005500Z
DTSTAMP:20250814T224500Z
UID:lKM7Naobjc
DESCRIPTION:Duration: 106 mins (1h46m)\n\nThe definitive tale of Jeff Buck
 ley\, the rising young star with an otherworldly voice whose sudden death 
 at age 30\, after the release of his critically acclaimed debut album "Gra
 ce\," shocked the world. Told through never-before-seen footage from Buckl
 ey’s archives and intimate accounts. Includes 26 minutes of exclusive\, 
 remastered footage from a previously unreleased solo performance filmed Fe
 bruary 19\, 1994\, screening immediately after the film:Very few were fort
 unate enough to witness Jeff Buckley live\, but those who did often descri
 bed it as transcendent\, jaw-dropping\, and emotionally shattering. As par
 t of the theatrical release of It’s Never Over: Jeff Buckley\, Magnolia 
 Pictures will proudly present 26 minutes of exclusive\, remastered footage
  from a rare solo performance at The Middle East in Cambridge\, MA\, filme
 d on February 19\, 1994. This previously unreleased set will screen immedi
 ately following the film\, offering both longtime fans and newcomers a rar
 e opportunity to experience Jeff Buckley’s raw\, unfiltered brilliance.\
 n\nhttps://www.siff.net/cinema/in-theaters/its-never-over-jeff-buckley
LOCATION:SIFF Cinema Uptown House 2\, 511 Queen Anne Avenue North
END:VEVENT
